Page</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI Agents</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>Security</category> <category>agentic-web</category> <category>ai-agents</category> <category>attestation</category> <category>auth</category> <category>did</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>knowledge-context-protocol</category> <category>open-source</category> <category>trust</category> <description>The agentic web has no login page — so the only knowledge agents can consume is what publishers give away. KCP v0.22 and v0.23 add the missing half of the trust model: who may consume knowledge, and how they prove it.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/04/the-agentic-web-has-no-login-page/</link> <pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/04/the-agentic-web-has-no-login-page/</guid> </item> <item> <title>One Agent&#39;s Journey Through the Whole Protocol</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI Agents</category> <category>Architecture</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>agentic-web</category> <category>attestation</category> <category>discovery</category> <category>federation</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>knowledge-context-protocol</category> <category>open-source</category> <category>org-hub</category> <category>temporal</category> <category>trust</category> <description>v0.24 shipped today — the enterprise front door. Twenty-four versions in six months, and every layer now has a job: discovery, meaning, trust, time, identity, federation. One agent&#39;s traversal through the whole protocol, annotated.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/04/one-agents-journey-through-the-whole-protocol/</link> <pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/04/one-agents-journey-through-the-whole-protocol/</guid> </item> <item> <title>The CI Pipeline Is the Agent&#39;s Nervous System</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>ai</category> <category>architecture</category> <category>ci</category> <category>devops</category> <category>exocortex</category> <category>testing</category> <description>When the agent writes code that passes locally but fails in CI, it&#39;s not a test problem. It&#39;s a nervous system problem.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/02/the-ci-pipeline-is-the-agents-nervous-system/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/02/the-ci-pipeline-is-the-agents-nervous-system/</guid> </item> <item> <title>The Third Test Harness</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>ai</category> <category>architecture</category> <category>exocortex</category> <category>playwright</category> <category>testing</category> <category>verification</category> <description>Unit tests catch logic bugs. Integration tests catch assembly bugs. The third harness catches specification drift — and it&#39;s the one AI-augmented teams need most.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/02/the-third-test-harness/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/02/the-third-test-harness/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Against the Swarm</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>agents</category> <category>ai</category> <category>architecture</category> <category>exocortex</category> <category>multi-agent</category> <description>The industry is building swarms of competing agents. The value is in one agent that knows your work.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/01/against-the-swarm/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/01/against-the-swarm/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Three Hooks That Give Claude Code Memory</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>ExoCortex</category> <category>claude-code</category> <category>episodic-memory</category> <category>exocortex</category> <category>hooks</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>open-source</category> <category>prompt-hygiene</category> <category>skills</category> <description>Three passive hooks that give Claude Code memory, routing, and hygiene — without changing how you work. The session amnesia problem, and how to fix it at the prompt boundary.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/28/three-hooks-that-give-claude-code-memory/</link> <pubDate>Sun, 28 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/28/three-hooks-that-give-claude-code-memory/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Production Scars Are Architecture</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>ExoCortex</category> <category>ai-agents</category> <category>hooks</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>mechanical-governance</category> <category>production</category> <category>security</category> <description>Six architectural lessons from running an autonomous AI agent in production. Each scar is a failure category surprising enough to force mechanical change. Prose governance didn&#39;t work — here&#39;s what did.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/23/production-scars-are-architecture/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/23/production-scars-are-architecture/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Your AI Agent Does Not Know the Law (and How to Fix That)</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Compliance</category> <category>ai-agents</category> <category>benchmarking</category> <category>compliance</category> <category>gdpr</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>knowledge-infrastructure</category> <category>python</category> <category>typescript</category> <description>Your AI agent will confidently tell a customer they&#39;re GDPR-compliant when they&#39;re not. Here&#39;s the architecture that fixes that.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/22/your-ai-agent-does-not-know-the-law-and-how-to-fix-that/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 22 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/22/your-ai-agent-does-not-know-the-law-and-how-to-fix-that/</guid> </item> <item> <title>The Zombie in the Basement</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Architecture</category> <category>ai-agents</category> <category>architecture</category> <category>documentation</category> <category>graph</category> <category>migrations</category> <category>verification</category> <description>Static architecture catalogs document what someone knew at a point in time. Betonix GmbH thought they had 23 database connections. They had 52. The migration nearly shipped that delta.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/19/the-zombie-in-the-basement/</link> <pubDate>Fri, 19 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/19/the-zombie-in-the-basement/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Google&#39;s Open Knowledge Format and the problems it deliberately doesn&#39;t solve</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI Agents</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>ai-agents</category> <category>google</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>knowledge-format</category> <category>okf</category> <category>temporal</category> <category>trust</category> <description>Google&#39;s Open Knowledge Format standardises content packaging for agents but stops before trust, temporality, and governance. KCP covers exactly that territory.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/17/googles-open-knowledge-format-and-the-problems-it-deliberately-doesnt-solve/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 17 Jun 2026 18:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/17/googles-open-knowledge-format-and-the-problems-it-deliberately-doesnt-solve/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Sixteen Versions of Metadata Nobody Read</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>compound-developer</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>practitioner-notes</category> <category>regulatory-compliance</category> <category>synthesis</category> <category>temporal</category> <category>verification</category> <description>63 regulatory manifests with full KCP v0.21 metadata -- hashes, signatures, temporal validity. Then a benchmark showed agents were not reading any of it.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/14/sixteen-versions-of-metadata-nobody-read/</link> <pubDate>Sun, 14 Jun 2026 14:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/14/sixteen-versions-of-metadata-nobody-read/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Discoverable Is Not Navigable</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>ExoCortex</category> <category>agentic-writing</category> <category>agents-reading</category> <category>exocortex</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>knowledge-infrastructure</category> <category>meta</category> <category>sdd</category> <description>Discoverable is not navigable. Extracting 38 Dutch obligation units from inline YAML to standalone text made content agent-traversable, not just findable.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/14/discoverable-is-not-navigable/</link> <pubDate>Sun, 14 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/14/discoverable-is-not-navigable/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Stale Knowledge Is Worse Than No Knowledge: KCP v0.19 and v0.20 Close the Temporal Gap</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>ai-context</category> <category>bi-temporal</category> <category>compliance</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>temporal</category> <description>Stale knowledge is worse than none. KCP v0.19 adds bi-temporal validity and supersession links; v0.20 adds as_of queries for point-in-time compliance.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/12/stale-knowledge-is-worse-than-no-knowledge-kcp-v019-and-v020-close-the-temporal-gap/</link> <pubDate>Fri, 12 Jun 2026 17:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/12/stale-knowledge-is-worse-than-no-knowledge-kcp-v019-and-v020-close-the-temporal-gap/</guid> </item> <item> <title>2026 06 12 kcp 0.18 unit integrity</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>ai-security</category> <category>content-integrity</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>supply-chain-security</category> <category>trust</category> <description>KCP v0.18 adds per-unit content hashes and origin evidence. Signing the manifest proves the map is authentic; hashes prove the territory matches.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/12/2026-06-12-kcp-018-unit-integrity/</link> <pubDate>Fri, 12 Jun 2026 14:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/12/2026-06-12-kcp-018-unit-integrity/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Down the Rabbit Hole: How a 33-Tool-Call Bug Became a Knowledge Standard</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>ai-agents</category> <category>compliance</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>knowledge-context-protocol</category> <category>mcp</category> <category>open-source</category> <category>sdd</category> <category>skill-driven-development</category> <category>trust</category> <description>KCP started when a 33-tool-call bug revealed agents waste their budget on discovery. Six months later: a knowledge standard with trust and governance.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/12/down-the-rabbit-hole-how-a-33-tool-call-bug-became-a-knowledge-standard/</link> <pubDate>Fri, 12 Jun 2026 11:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/12/down-the-rabbit-hole-how-a-33-tool-call-bug-became-a-knowledge-standard/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Beyond RAG: How KCP 0.16--0.17 Give Agents Trustworthy, Self-Describing Knowledge</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>ai-security</category> <category>content-structure</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>mcp</category> <category>rag</category> <category>trust</category> <description>KCP v0.16 adds cryptographic signing and trust tiers. v0.17 adds content structure metadata and subtractive audience filtering for precision retrieval.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/12/beyond-rag-how-kcp-016--017-give-agents-trustworthy-self-describing-knowledge/</link> <pubDate>Fri, 12 Jun 2026 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/12/beyond-rag-how-kcp-016--017-give-agents-trustworthy-self-describing-knowledge/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Explorative Development</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Skill-Driven Development</category> <category>agentic-engineering</category> <category>ai-productivity</category> <category>compound-developer</category> <category>explorative-development</category> <category>fear-driven-development</category> <category>hypothesis-driven</category> <category>practitioner-notes</category> <category>simulation</category> <category>verification</category> <description>Before writing production code, run a fictional organisation through two years of using the feature. Front-load discovery before the first commit.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/11/explorative-development/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 11 Jun 2026 18:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/11/explorative-development/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Organized Truths</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Skill-Driven Development</category> <category>agentic-engineering</category> <category>ai-productivity</category> <category>compound-developer</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>knowledge-infrastructure</category> <category>practitioner-notes</category> <category>regulatory-compliance</category> <category>verification</category> <description>Catch an agent making a false compliance claim once, encode the verification as a skill, and every future session inherits the check. Organised truths scale.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/11/organized-truths/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 11 Jun 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/11/organized-truths/</guid> </item> <item> <title>False Alarms and False Assurances</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Skill-Driven Development</category> <category>agentic-engineering</category> <category>ai-productivity</category> <category>code-review</category> <category>compound-developer</category> <category>fear-driven-development</category> <category>practitioner-notes</category> <category>verification</category> <description>An agent claimed an API had no authentication. Four minutes of reading proved otherwise. Verifying agent assertions is the non-negotiable skill.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/11/false-alarms-and-false-assurances/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 11 Jun 2026 14:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/11/false-alarms-and-false-assurances/</guid> </item> </channel> </rss>